# Hermodr (valheim-bot.py / valheim-bot.service) -- the Discord Q&A bot and the restart-approval
# relay. TEMPLATE: every value below ships empty; real values live only in /etc/valheim-bot.env
# on the VM. Install it mode 0640 root:valheim-bot -- systemd reads EnvironmentFile as root
# before the service drops privileges to the unprivileged valheim-bot user (see
# valheim-bot.service's User=/Group=), so a non-world-readable file here is fine, and preferred.
#
# This file used to be part of /etc/valheim-alert.env; it split out because the alert/medals/
# digest scripts need DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL and this process does not, and should not hold a
# credential it never uses. See valheim-alert.env's header for the other side of that split.
#
# Empty DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN means the service logs a line and exits 0 immediately (no crash loop);
# nothing else below matters until it is set. See azure/README.md "Hermodr" for full setup and
# the security model.
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=
# The only channel Hermodr answers Q&A in. Prefer the numeric id (right-click the channel in
# Discord with Developer Mode on > Copy Channel ID) over the name -- an id can't be renamed out
# from under it. HERMODR_CHANNEL_NAME is only a fallback, resolved once at startup by exact name.
HERMODR_CHANNEL_ID=
HERMODR_CHANNEL_NAME=
# The guild both HERMODR_CHANNEL_ID above and RESTART_APPROVAL_CHANNEL_ID below belong to. Every
# restart-approval interaction is checked against this id server-side, even though Discord already
# scopes interactions to a guild -- see valheim-bot.py's is_authorized_approver().
# Obtain: enable Developer Mode in Discord settings, then right-click the server icon > Copy Server ID.
HERMODR_GUILD_ID=
# Azure AI Foundry chat-completions endpoint and model deployment name. Auth is the VM's managed
# identity (no API key stored anywhere) -- swap HERMODR_AI_MODEL alone to point at a different
# deployment; leave HERMODR_AI_ENDPOINT unset to use the ai-valheim project's default endpoint.
HERMODR_AI_ENDPOINT=
HERMODR_AI_MODEL=
# Log file path. Leave unset to use the default, /var/log/hermodr/hermodr.log --
# LogsDirectory=hermodr in valheim-bot.service makes systemd create that directory owned by the
# service's own user before start, so the de-rooted bot can write there without a broader
# /var/log grant. This is a new path: it used to be /var/log/hermodr.log (flat, root-owned).
HERMODR_LOG=

# --- Restart approval (see PLAN-v5.md "The spool" / "Request state machine") ---
# A SEPARATE, role-restricted Discord channel -- never HERMODR_CHANNEL_ID above -- so non-hall
# members never even see the Approve/Deny buttons. Numeric channel id only.
RESTART_APPROVAL_CHANNEL_ID=
# Numeric Discord role id (Server Settings > Roles > the role > ... > Copy Role ID with Developer
# Mode on). Never a role name -- names can be renamed or duplicated, ids cannot. Anyone with
# Manage Roles in the guild can grant themselves this role, so configuring it means Discord
# server-admin implies restart-approval authority; that is accepted, see PLAN-v5's "honest limits".
RESTART_APPROVER_ROLE_ID=
# This feature fails closed: if HERMODR_GUILD_ID above, RESTART_APPROVAL_CHANNEL_ID, or
# RESTART_APPROVER_ROLE_ID is left empty, the bot never reads the restart spool, never posts an
# approval request, and never writes a verdict -- it logs one line explaining why and stops
# there. It never falls back to an unrestricted channel or an unchecked role.
